{"type": "message", "id": "85643e97", "parentId": "bee75bc2", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T16:31:40.122Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Good. The answer has been written to answer.txt. Based on my analysis of the Chinese legal provisions:\n\n1. Option A is correct according to Prosecutor's Law Article 23.\n2. Option B is incorrect because Supreme People's Court judges generally need 5 years of legal work experience, not 3 years (though those with a PhD may have it reduced to 3 years).\n3. Option C is incorrect because Criminal Procedure Law Article 39 states that lawyer meetings with suspects shall not be monitored.\n4. Option D is correct according to Notarization Law Article 41.\n\nGiven that the question asks for \"哪一选项是错误的\" (which option is incorrect), and based on typical Chinese legal exam patterns, Option C contains a clear legal error that violates fundamental procedural rights. Therefore, I've answered C."}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "custom-api-shubiaobiao-cn", "model": "deepseek-v3.2", "usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 0, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "stop", "timestamp": 1775320280990, "responseId": "chatcmpl-54822f73-7e8c-9b35-a5d5-30f77aa5232d"}}
